IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `taa-types`
IMPORT `taa-s55`

-- Tax Administration Act 1994 — GOAL 2: RETURNS AND THE TIME BAR.
--
--   "Must the person file a return; by when; to when may time be extended
--    through a tax agent; and until when may the Commissioner increase the
--    assessment?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1994_166.txt — ss 33, 37,
-- 108; Income Tax Act 2007 s YE 1(7).

§ `Goal 2 — returns and the time bar`

-- s 33(1) "In each tax year, a person, other than a person who derives only
-- exempt income, must file a return of income for a tax year".
@ref s 33(1)
GIVEN f IS A Filer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must file a return of income` f IF
    NOT f's `derives only exempt income`

-- Income Tax Act 2007, s YE 1(7): a late balance date is an approved income
-- year ending "in a date between 1 April and the following 30 September".
@ref Income Tax Act 2007 s YE 1(7)
GIVEN f IS A Filer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a late balance date` f IF
    CONSIDER f's `approved income year ends on`
    WHEN JUST ends THEN DATE_MONTH ends AT LEAST 4 AND DATE_MONTH ends AT MOST 9
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 37 "(1) The annual returns of income ... shall be furnished ...: (a) in
-- the case of any taxpayer with a late balance date, not later than the
-- seventh of the month which is the fourth month after the end of the
-- taxpayer's corresponding income year: (b) in all other cases, not later
-- than 7 July in each year."
@ref s 37(1); Income Tax Act 2007 s YE 1(7)
GIVEN f IS A Filer  @desc The tax year and any approved income year end
GIVETH A DATE
`the unextended due date for the return of` f MEANS
    IF   `has a late balance date` f
    THEN CONSIDER f's `approved income year ends on`
         WHEN JUST ends THEN Date 7 (DATE_MONTH fourth) (DATE_YEAR fourth)
             WHERE fourth MEANS `add months` (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH ends) (DATE_YEAR ends)) 4
         WHEN NOTHING THEN Date 7 7 (f's `tax year ending 31 March`)
    ELSE Date 7 7 (f's `tax year ending 31 March`)

-- s 37 "(5) For the purposes of subsections (3) and (4),— (a) where the return
-- ... is a return for a year ending on 31 March, the time ... shall not be
-- extended ... later than the 31 March that immediately succeeds that 31
-- March: (b) where ... a return for a year ending with the date of the annual
-- balance ..., (i) where that date is between 30 September and the next
-- succeeding 31 March, not ... later than the 31 March next succeeding the 31
-- March that immediately succeeds that date: (ii) where that date is between
-- 31 March and the next succeeding 1 October, not ... later than the 31 March
-- that immediately succeeds that date." "Between" is read exclusively of the
-- dates named (fork F2).
@ref s 37(4)-(5)
GIVEN f IS A Filer  @desc The tax year and any approved income year end
GIVETH A DATE
`the unextended latest extended due date for the return of` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `approved income year ends on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN standard
    WHEN JUST ends THEN
        IF   DATE_MONTH ends EQUALS 3 AND DATE_DAY ends EQUALS 31
        THEN Date 31 3 (DATE_YEAR ends PLUS 1)
        ELSE IF   DATE_MONTH ends AT LEAST 4 AND DATE_MONTH ends AT MOST 9
             THEN Date 31 3 (DATE_YEAR ends PLUS 1)
             ELSE Date 31 3 (firstMarch PLUS 1)
             WHERE firstMarch MEANS IF DATE_MONTH ends AT LEAST 10 THEN DATE_YEAR ends PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR ends
    WHERE
        standard MEANS Date 31 3 (f's `tax year ending 31 March` PLUS 1)

-- s 108 "(1) ... if— (a) a taxpayer furnishes an income tax return and an
-- assessment has been made; and (b) 4 years have passed from the end of the
-- tax year in which the taxpayer provides the tax return,— the Commissioner
-- may not amend the assessment so as to increase the amount assessed ...
-- (2) If ... a tax return ... (a) is fraudulent or wilfully misleading; or
-- (b) does not mention income which is of a particular nature or was derived
-- from a particular source, ... the Commissioner may amend the assessment at
-- any time".
@ref s 108(1)-(2)
GIVEN filed IS A DATE  @desc The day the return was provided
      fraud IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the return was fraudulent or wilfully misleading, or omitted income of a particular nature or source
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the unextended last day to increase the assessment, return provided` filed `, fraud or omission` fraud MEANS
    IF   fraud
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (Date 31 3 (yearEnds PLUS 4))
    WHERE
        yearEnds MEANS IF DATE_MONTH filed AT LEAST 4 THEN DATE_YEAR filed PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR filed

-- Legislation Act 2019 s 55 (applied 2026-10-17 at the user's direction): a
-- return due on a non-working day may be filed on the next working day.
@ref s 37(1); Legislation Act 2019 s 55
@export The due date for an annual return of income under s 37(1) of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ): 7 July after the tax year ends; for a taxpayer with a late balance date (an approved income year ending between 1 April and 30 September), the 7th of the 4th month after the income year ends; a due date that is not a working day runs to the next working day (Legislation Act 2019 s 55). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A Filer  @desc The tax year and any approved income year end
GIVETH A DATE
`the due date for the return of` f MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (`the unextended due date for the return of` f)

-- Legislation Act 2019 s 55 (applied 2026-10-17 at the user's direction): a
-- return due on a non-working day may be filed on the next working day.
@ref s 37(4)-(5); Legislation Act 2019 s 55
@export The latest date to which the time for filing a return may be extended through a tax agent under s 37(4)-(5) of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ): the 31 March after the tax year's 31 March; for another approved balance date, the second 31 March after a date from October to March, or the first 31 March after a date from April to September; if not a working day, the next working day (Legislation Act 2019 s 55). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A Filer  @desc The tax year and any approved income year end
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest extended due date for the return of` f MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (`the unextended latest extended due date for the return of` f)

-- Legislation Act 2019 s 55 (applied 2026-10-17): the time bar's last day,
-- if not a working day, runs to the next working day (fork S55).
@ref s 108; Legislation Act 2019 s 55
@export The last day the Commissioner may amend an income tax assessment to increase it under s 108 of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ): 31 March (or the next working day, Legislation Act 2019 s 55), 4 years after the end of the tax year in which the return was provided; none if the return was fraudulent or wilfully misleading or omitted income of a particular nature or source. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN filed IS A DATE  @desc The day the return was provided
      fraud IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the return was fraudulent or wilfully misleading, or omitted income of a particular nature or source
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to increase the assessment, return provided` filed `, fraud or omission` fraud MEANS
    `the last day under s 55, if any, for a deadline of` (`the unextended last day to increase the assessment, return provided` filed `, fraud or omission` fraud)
